IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- The source is a plain-text rendering (SCJA1969.txt), not the official text. Layer 1: the law, objectively; every name begins with the label of its provision.
-- scja2-part5-ca-general.l4: Part 5 (Court of Appeal), Division 1, General: ss 48 to 52 (President and Vice-Presidents, jurisdiction, composition, decisions, sittings).
-- JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (scja2)").
-- Twin: ss 30-34 and ss 48-52 say the same thing about the two courts; each section is encoded on its own (ruling E1, option C) with the wording kept alike.

§ `Part 5, Division 1 -- General`

§§ `s 48 -- President and Vice-Presidents`

-- src:2880 | 48.—(1) The Chief Justice is the President of the Court of Appeal
-- src:2881 | and may appoint one or more Vice‑Presidents of the Court of Appeal
-- src:2882 | from among the Justices of the Court of Appeal.
@ref s 48(1) (src:2880-2882)
GIVEN office IS A `Kind of Judge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(1) the Judge is the President of the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF office EQUALS `Chief Justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Chief Justice is the President of the Court of Appeal"; the text says nothing of any other Judge being the President
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2880 | 48.—(1) The Chief Justice is the President of the Court of Appeal
-- src:2881 | and may appoint one or more Vice‑Presidents of the Court of Appeal
-- src:2882 | from among the Justices of the Court of Appeal.
@ref s 48(1) (src:2880-2882)
GIVEN office IS A `Kind of Judge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(1) the Chief Justice may appoint the Judge to be a Vice-President of the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF office EQUALS `Justice of the Court of Appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to appoint Vice-Presidents "from among the Justices of the Court of Appeal"; the text does not say whether anyone else may be appointed
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2888 | (a) the most senior Supreme Court Judge, as determined by
-- src:2889 | section 4, is to preside; and
@ref s 48(2)(a) (src:2888-2889)
GIVEN judge IS A Judge
      `s 4 the most senior Supreme Court Judge among those sitting` IS A MAYBE Judge
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(2)(a) the Judge is to preside in a sitting of the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4 the most senior Supreme Court Judge among those sitting`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who is the most senior Supreme Court Judge is determined by section 4, which another part of this encoding answers (PLAN.md seam 12)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST senior THEN
        IF senior's `reference for this person` EQUALS judge's `reference for this person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text names the most senior Supreme Court Judge as the one who presides and does not say anything of another Judge
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2891 | (b) if there is no Supreme Court Judge, the Chief Justice is to
-- src:2892 | appoint a person to preside.
@ref s 48(2)(b) (src:2891-2892)
GIVEN `there is a Supreme Court Judge sitting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(2)(b) the Chief Justice is to appoint a person to preside in a sitting of the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF NOT `there is a Supreme Court Judge sitting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if there is no Supreme Court Judge" -- the "if" is not met when a Supreme Court Judge is sitting
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 49 -- Jurisdiction, general`

-- src:2903 | 49.—(1) The Court of Appeal has the civil jurisdiction mentioned
-- src:2904 | in section 53, the criminal jurisdiction mentioned in section 60D and
-- src:2905 | the jurisdiction to deal with any application or action that is to be dealt
-- src:2906 | with by the Court of Appeal as is provided in Division 4 of this Part.
@ref s 49(1) (src:2903-2906)
GIVEN `s 53(2) the matter is one of the matters of the civil jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 60D the matter is one of the matters of the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Division 4 provides that the application or action is to be dealt with by the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(1) the Court of Appeal has jurisdiction over the matter` MEANS
    IF `s 53(2) the matter is one of the matters of the civil jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `s 60D the matter is one of the matters of the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `Division 4 provides that the application or action is to be dealt with by the Court of Appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection says what the Court of Appeal "has" and does not close the list with "only"; a matter in none of the three limbs is not decided by it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2910 | (2) The Court of Appeal has, in an appeal and for any purpose
-- src:2911 | related to an appeal, all the jurisdiction and powers of the court or
-- src:2912 | tribunal from which the appeal was brought.
@ref s 49(2) (src:2910-2912)
GIVEN `it is an appeal, or a purpose relating to an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is one that the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought has` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(2) the Court of Appeal has the jurisdiction or power of the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought` MEANS
    IF `it is an appeal, or a purpose relating to an appeal` AND `the power is one that the court or tribunal from which the appeal was brought has`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "in an appeal and for any purpose relating to an appeal" and of the jurisdiction and powers of the court or tribunal appealed from
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2916 | (3) The Court of Appeal may decide any question that needs to be
-- src:2917 | decided to do justice in any case before it.
@ref s 49(3) (src:2916-2917)
GIVEN `the question needs to be decided to do justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question arises in a case before the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(3) the Court of Appeal may decide the question` MEANS
    IF `the question needs to be decided to do justice` AND `the question arises in a case before the Court of Appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "any question that needs to be decided to do justice in any case before it"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 50 -- Composition, general`

-- src:2923 | 50.—(1) Subject to this Act, the jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal
-- src:2924 | is to be exercised by 3 or any greater uneven number of Judges.
@ref s 50(1) (src:2923-2924)
GIVEN `the number of Judges who exercise the jurisdiction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(1) the number of Judges is one that the subsection provides for` MEANS
    IF `the number of Judges who exercise the jurisdiction` AT LEAST 3 AND (`the number of Judges who exercise the jurisdiction` MODULO 2) EQUALS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to this Act" -- other provisions of the Act allow other numbers (ss 54(1), 58(3) and (4)), and the subsection does not say in terms that another number is invalid
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2928 | (2) A Judge must not sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide any
-- src:2929 | appeal from a decision made by the Judge, or any matter related to
-- src:2930 | such an appeal.
@ref s 50(2) (src:2928-2930)
GIVEN `the matter is an appeal from a decision made by the Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is related to such an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(2) the Judge may sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter is an appeal from a decision made by the Judge` OR `the matter is related to such an appeal`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A Judge must not sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide any appeal from a decision made by the Judge, or any matter related to such an appeal."
        JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition reaches only an appeal from the Judge's own decision and matters related to it; the subsection is silent on any other matter
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The prohibition is derived from the answer above (ruling N2): the text names its bearer, "A Judge".
DECLARE `s 50(2) party` IS ONE OF `s 50(2) the Judge who made the decision appealed from`
DECLARE `s 50(2) act` IS ONE OF `s 50(2) sits in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the appeal`

-- src:2928 | (2) A Judge must not sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide any
-- src:2929 | appeal from a decision made by the Judge, or any matter related to
-- src:2930 | such an appeal.
@ref s 50(2) (src:2928-2930)
`s 50(2) the prohibition on the Judge` MEANS
    PARTY `s 50(2) the Judge who made the decision appealed from`
    SHANT `s 50(2) sits in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the appeal`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 50(2) the Judge who made the decision appealed from` BECAUSE "a Judge sat in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide an appeal from the Judge's own decision"

#TRACE `s 50(2) the prohibition on the Judge` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 50(2) the Judge who made the decision appealed from` DOES `s 50(2) sits in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the appeal` AT 1

-- src:2934 | (3) Section 10A applies in relation to proceedings before the Court
-- src:2935 | of Appeal as it applies in relation to proceedings before the General
-- src:2936 | Division.
@ref s 50(3) (src:2934-2936)
GIVEN `s 10A the court may summon assessors` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(3) the Court of Appeal may summon assessors as section 10A allows` MEANS
    -- section 10A "applies in relation to proceedings before the Court of Appeal as it applies in relation to proceedings before the General Division": the answer is the one section 10A gives for this court (PLAN.md seam 13), passed through unchanged
    `s 10A the court may summon assessors`

§§ `s 51 -- Decisions how made`

-- src:2942 | 51.—(1) A decision of the Court of Appeal is to be made in
-- src:2943 | accordance with the opinion of the majority of the Judges hearing the
-- src:2944 | case.
@ref s 51(1) (src:2942-2944)
GIVEN `how the Judges divided` IS A `Split of opinion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(1) the decision goes the way of the opinion of the majority of the Judges hearing the case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- the answer is JUST TRUE where the majority are for the claim, appeal or application
        IF `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` GREATER THAN `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges against it` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in accordance with the opinion of the majority" -- the decision follows a majority against the claim, appeal or application
        IF `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` LESS THAN `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges against it` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an even division has no majority; subsection (2) deals with an appeal or application
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2948 | (2) An appeal or application to the Court of Appeal is to be
-- src:2949 | dismissed if the Judges hearing the appeal or application are evenly
-- src:2950 | divided.
@ref s 51(2) (src:2948-2950)
GIVEN `how the Judges divided` IS A `Split of opinion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(2) the appeal or application is dismissed because the Judges hearing it are evenly divided` MEANS
    IF `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` EQUALS `how the Judges divided`'s `Judges against it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Judges hearing the appeal or application are evenly divided" -- the "if" is not met
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 52 -- Sittings`

-- src:2963 | (a) is to sit on such dates and at such places as the Chief Justice
-- src:2964 | may from time to time appoint; and
@ref s 52(1)(a) (src:2963-2964)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice has appointed the date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(1)(a) the date is one that the Chief Justice appointed` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Justice has appointed the date`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Court of Appeal "is to sit on such dates ... as the Chief Justice may from time to time appoint"; the text does not say that a sitting on another date is invalid
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2963 | (a) is to sit on such dates and at such places as the Chief Justice
-- src:2964 | may from time to time appoint; and
@ref s 52(1)(a) (src:2963-2964)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice has appointed the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(1)(a) the place is one that the Chief Justice appointed` MEANS
    IF `the Chief Justice has appointed the place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Court of Appeal "is to sit ... at such places as the Chief Justice may from time to time appoint"; the text does not say that a sitting at another place is invalid
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2966 | (b) may sit on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, or during
-- src:2967 | a vacation, if the Chief Justice so appoints.
@ref s 52(1)(b) (src:2966-2967)
GIVEN `the day is a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, or falls during a vacation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Chief Justice so appoints` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(1)(b) the Court of Appeal may sit on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks only of a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, or a vacation
        IF NOT `the day is a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, or falls during a vacation` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Chief Justice so appoints` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Chief Justice so appoints" -- the "if" is not met
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:2971 | (2) The Chief Justice may cancel or postpone a sitting appointed
-- src:2972 | under subsection (1).
@ref s 52(2) (src:2971-2972)
GIVEN `the sitting was appointed under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(2) the Chief Justice may cancel or postpone the sitting` MEANS
    IF `the sitting was appointed under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "a sitting appointed under subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING
